WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.070
Infinite Ryvius

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:48.810
From an endless sorrow to somewhere else

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:49.780
What...

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.120
What happened?

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:57.080
Infinite Ryvius

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:04.690
If you're going to walk, right here will be fine

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.700
Although loneliness...

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.030
...can sometimes be unbearable

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:20.270
There's the benefit of not hurting anyone...

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:25.350
...and the benefit of not being exposed...

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:28.320
...and hurt by others as well

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:35.850
At the opposite side of the frozen sea...

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.630
...the dream and the reality...

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:43.260
...that you saw cross paths

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:46.960
Some light is shed...

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.540
...but how it is done is unknown...

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:58.780
...so that we can go to a different place

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:06.780
The things I want have no shape

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:15.190
Tear the final universe, today until tomorrow

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:29.070
Ring of Ryvius

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.040
I-I can't get this off!

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:34.880
Hey...!

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.040
I wouldn't want to be seen like this.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:38.920
You've got a point.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:42.490
<i>All blocks, please check machinery to</i>
<i>ensure everything is in working order.</i>

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:45.030
<i>People with injuries should make</i>
<i>their way to the hangar in Block D.</i>

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.790
Can I have a first aid box over here too?

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:49.060
Hey! Emergency!

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.570
Wait in that line!

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.200
Oww... Can't you be a little gentler?

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.470
I'm doing my best!

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:55.100
Have Kelly look at it.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:58.570
I've got my hands full.
How many more are there?

00:02:58.570 --> 00:02:59.580
About fifteen.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.380
I haven't had a thing to eat.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.510
Tape this up tightly.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:04.210
My figure's all smashed up.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:06.180
Same here.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:08.580
Daddy.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.250
A complete one G?

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:13.820
Throughout all of Liebel?

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:17.230
In addition, it's moving
steadily in one direction.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.830
I'd understand it if we'd been
accelerating at 1 G, but that isn't the case.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:23.070
Maybe it's a built in emergency function.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:24.900
So that's what it is.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:30.610
Liebe Delta's course was changed by the
people who tried to take over the bridge...

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.940
...but the situation since then
is too irregular to figure out.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:33.880
Yes.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.880
Not only has this ship and
Liebe Delta survived Sere 3...

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.080
...we proceeded regardless of our
failure in our flight approach.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:45.820
And the fact this ship is
maintaining a one G force...!

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:47.020
I got it!

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.150
This Liebel has a hidden secret!

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.860
Like what?

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.560
Probably a really awesome secret.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.230
Hey, everyone!

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.200
Kreis just found something incredible.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.610
They've caused us great trouble.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:11.080
Wh-What a relief. I was
nervous coming in here alone.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:12.950
We're not here to protect you.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:18.750
R-Right. Oh, by the way, my name
is Good Turtleland the Third.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.280
If there's anything you need...!

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:23.260
Don't...!

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.230
Don't scare me like that!

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:29.100
You've gotta be joking, with
a name like "The Third".

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.270
You look more like a
"Charlie", whaddaya say?

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:34.240
Right on.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.770
Y-You think so?

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.550
Bye now. Don't forget to inform me
whenever you're interrogating, Charlie.

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.510
We'll let 'em suffer, Charlie.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.840
My name's not Charlie.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.060
Bye-bye, Charlie.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.020
Charlie, Charlie.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.230
I can live with that.

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:02.800
Come to think of it, the guys who attacked
the bridge were soldiers, weren't they?

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.700
They were outfitted like soldiers.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.640
What do you think they were after?

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.300
I haven't got a clue.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:09.870
Um...

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.610
...I can find my way alone from here.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:12.840
Will you be all right?

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.910
Yes. Thank you.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.880
You sure you can manage alone?

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.210
Should you have a girlfriend,
I wouldn't want to upset her.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.180
Huh?

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:23.650
What girlfriend?

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:27.120
Aren't you going after her? You've
been given the chance to meet her...

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:28.920
...why not ask her out or something?

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:30.660
This isn't the time for that!

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:31.960
So you'd like to.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.730
- No!
- Ikumi!

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:35.960
Oh, Kozue! I hope you didn't get hurt!

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.300
I'm okay. I'm always lucky that way.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.270
Perhaps that extra weight helped.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.910
You and your mouth. How
can you be so tactless?

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:45.870
Kouji.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:47.410
Hi.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:51.250
You were with Zwei, right? What's
going on with this gravity?

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.080
They're checking it out right now.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.450
Is it true that the instructors are dead?

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:57.120
It'd be better if you didn't ask.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.520
Gotcha.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:02.590
I've been instructed not to talk about it.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:03.690
Let's go.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.230
B-Bye.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:07.200
Are you going out with him?

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:08.930
Who?

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.160
You and him.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:12.130
Am I wrong?

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.230
We've just been friends since childhood.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:20.310
I've forwarded the data.
Look on that screen.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:23.850
How pretty...!

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:27.470
Looks like a Navigational Solid.
I've never seen this style.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.980
Neither have I. It's quite advanced.

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:32.190
What does that have to do with anything?

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:36.620
It means that at some point, this Solid
has overwritten the main program.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:38.490
So how does that affect anything?

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:40.600
I'm showing it to you 'cause I don't know!

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:44.400
For your information, I've only pulled
about three percent of the whole thing.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:46.230
Three percent?

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:49.230
The rest is too difficult to decipher.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:51.740
This can't be.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:52.770
What is it?

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:56.210
No part of this Navigational
Solid is connected to Liebel.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:57.110
What?

00:06:57.110 --> 00:07:00.350
Which means we need to
learn a whole new system.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.320
You're right. Let's check the system.

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:09.690
What's this?

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:11.660
A blueprint of a new model?

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:14.130
It has the name of a ship.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:19.800
What's the present position of V.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:22.270
Sere one, 670.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:25.670
Communication will be
possible in about one minute.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:29.540
Contamination! Number two film of
23rd buffer zone surface is melting!

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:30.910
Grahp levels rising!

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:32.910
Average temperature of
outer walls, 740 anvils...

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.050
...continue applying coolant
until we reach Sere two, 500.

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:39.320
This is Captain Conrad of submersible
ship Tandel. Our mission has failed.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.950
Bratica's system... activation confirmed.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:48.490
We'll send a compressed file on Bratica's
estimated location. Get online using Zebra.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:51.330
May the fortunes of war smile upon you.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:04.880
<i>Test. Test.</i>

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:09.050
Why is Lucson talking?

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:10.890
Nobody else volunteered.

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.750
Hello everybody.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:17.490
I am leader of the second term Zwei class
of the Navigation Section, Lucson Hojo.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:21.430
We at Zwei consider everyone's
safety to be top priority.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:25.530
Despite operational difficulties, we
successfully escaped the Geduld Sea.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:26.870
What are you bragging about?

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:28.600
Who do you think you are?

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.010
We aren't here to listen to your speech!

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:33.180
- Where are the instructors?
- When will we be rescued?

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:35.180
So, let me explain...

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:37.380
How long will we be stuck here?

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:39.720
This violates the Minor's Protection Law!

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:41.580
Hurry up with your answer, idiot!

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.550
Yeah, hurry up!

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:49.560
<i>Sh-Shut up!</i>

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.060
Wh-What's so...

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.960
What's so funny?

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:03.070
Hey, you over there! And you
too! Who do you think I am...?

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:06.840
Everybody! We apologize for the delay
in updating you of the situation!

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:09.080
Then hurry with your explanation!

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:13.010
- You're avoiding the questions!
- That's right! Say something!

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:17.720
Please understand that we did
what we thought was necessary...

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:20.760
...believing that it would not
affect the ship's navigation.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:25.230
I will tell you what caused the accident,
and how we got the ship under control.

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:27.100
- This is very important.
- This is definitely a job for a woman.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:30.300
- <i>Please listen quietly until I am finished.</i>
- Talk like that could get you in trouble.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:34.670
During its dive, the course of Liebe
Delta was altered, leaving it in danger...

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.140
...of being crushed by external forces.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:38.470
It is clear that this was an act of sabotage.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:41.680
- What?
- Is she serious?

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:47.620
<i>We have no information on who planned</i>
<i>the crime, or why they did it.</i>

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:53.080
<i>What we do know is that we were</i>
<i>forced into a critical situation.</i>

00:09:54.690 --> 00:10:00.060
<i>We Zwei discovered this by chance</i>
<i>and brought you here to Liebel.</i>

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:04.520
<i>We made the decision to launch this ship</i>
<i>to escape from the falling Liebe Delta.</i>

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:09.700
<i>However, we experienced difficulties</i>
<i>in our flight preparation...</i>

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:14.270
<i>...and were faced with the reality of</i>
<i>being crushed along with Liebe Delta.</i>

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:20.140
R-Realizing the danger...

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:24.790
<i>...the instructors took on the task of</i>
<i>purging the surrounding facilities.</i>

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:28.590
<i>Thanks to their sacrifice, Liebe</i>
<i>Delta successfully decelerated...</i>

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:32.050
<i>...giving us additional</i>
<i>time to prepare to launch.</i>

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:38.050
- We've survived because...
- Are you saying the instructors are dead?

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:43.870
Yes. They all died in the line of duty.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:47.840
No mention that they were murdered.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.250
It's better that way.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:54.410
<i>Thanks to their noble sacrifice, we were</i>
<i>able to successfully launch this ship.</i>

00:10:54.920 --> 00:11:00.550
<i>Liebel is currently drifting at 27, 000</i>
<i>Zelares between Earth and Mars.</i>

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:09.260
Unfortunately we're not out of the woods.
Please observe the screen closest to you.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.430
<i>This is Liebel, where we are right now.</i>

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.640
What's this?

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:19.540
Isn't this a diagram of a spaceship?

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:21.810
Why is something attached to Liebel?

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:27.280
<i>As you can see...</i>

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:33.590
<i>...Liebel is attached to an unidentified</i>
<i>spaceship hidden within the central pillar.</i>

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:37.590
<i>We found this unknown ship</i>
<i>within the navigational program.</i>

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:40.230
<i>Its name is...!</i>

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.590
Ryvius.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:50.600
Infinite Ryvius

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:55.610
Infinite Ryvius

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:59.940
<i>Currently, Liebel's energy</i>
<i>is being supplied by Ryvius.</i>

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:04.240
<i>We assume that the 1 G we have now is</i>
<i>tied in with the features of Ryvius.</i>

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:09.560
<i>Liebel has been sending out a rescue</i>
<i>signal for the past five hours...</i>

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:12.360
<i>...but it is not wise to remain</i>
<i>in this unstable location.</i>

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:16.430
<i>Our best option is to move to Ryvius,</i>
<i>which has its own power source...</i>

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:17.460
<i>...and wait to be rescued there.</i>

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:22.970
Do not worry. Help will arrive. We ask
for your understanding and cooperation.

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:28.340
That went reasonably well.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:29.880
Yeah.

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:31.310
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:34.650
We will now hand out a Living
Plan, based on our manual.

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:40.280
<i>This is a guideline to help us live</i>
<i>together in harmony until help arrives.</i>

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:44.130
<i>Please understand that this plan is not</i>
<i>a list of instructions enforced by Zwei...</i>

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:45.990
<i>...but a tool to allow us all to survive.</i>

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:47.990
Who do they think they are, anyway?

00:12:56.570 --> 00:13:01.410
Received message, standard solar system
time, 1544, by way of Darjeeling wave.

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:04.510
We received a rescue signal from
the ship believed to be our target.

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:05.980
It matches the data from Tandel.

00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:10.080
Switch the plan to YS45.
We will suppress Bratica.

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:19.060
Huh?

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.260
Funny. We ended up in the same place.

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:23.230
What a strange bridge.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:26.530
The design is completely
different from the common bridge.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:29.990
But this is top class. I've always
wanted to be on a bridge like this.

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.230
This is nothing like our training bridge.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:34.770
Let's hurry and get this ship ready.

00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:37.050
Yeah. How's the air level?

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:39.070
Satisfactory. Where's the manual?

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:41.940
There is none. It must be online.

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:49.220
Oh, wow! It's not the latest, but
it's got memory space like crazy.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.120
This is even better than the one on Dione.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.620
Can't we board Ryvius yet?

00:13:57.130 --> 00:14:00.360
They say first we have to form teams
of four or five in the same program.

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:03.300
Guess they want us to
choose our own roommates.

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:05.040
Then it's decided for us, right?

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.880
Yes. Since we're all conductors.

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:09.110
Oze! Come join our group!

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:11.380
If you want only me, then forget it! Sorry!

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:13.810
Okay! Never mind!

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:15.680
Aren't you glad?

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:17.650
A-About what?

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:20.820
What do you think
you're doing? You fool!

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:23.150
Give the guy a break, Nicks!

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:25.730
Oh, hi Ikumi. What are you doing?

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:27.700
I'm looking for guys to form a team with.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:30.960
Is it just the two of you? Why not join us?

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:36.370
Sure. I don't mind.

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:38.400
Okay. Then it's decided.

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:41.410
Hi. Nice to meet you.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:45.640
I-I'm Akihiro Miyabi. I'm sixteen.

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:48.750
Oh, hi. Kouji Aiba. Sixteen.

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:50.720
I'm Nicks! Thirteen!

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:53.420
He's a hopeless brat, but his
operating skills are top notch.

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:54.990
I'm not a brat! Take this!

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:56.190
Hey, no warning?

00:14:56.190 --> 00:14:58.890
Sorry. He's foul-tongued,
but he's a great guy.

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:03.030
I'm impressed to see you with a girlfriend.
But not too impressed with your partner.

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:04.670
H-He really is a good guy.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.700
I believe you.

00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:11.100
To the many who sacrificed their lives
to protect us and the Liebel, salute!

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:23.070
<i>Internal check of the ship is complete.</i>
<i>We will now open the hatch to Ryvius.</i>

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:29.590
Let's hurry.

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:30.860
Calm down.

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:32.430
Definitely the center of attention.

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:34.030
He acts like a kid.

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:38.170
But I like the fact he's full of
energy. Just like Kouji some years ago.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:39.730
Hurry! Hurry!

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:41.790
We should've come here in the first place.

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:50.600
With the prayers of Aisha, and a heart that
goes deeper than charity, this ordeal...!

00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:55.910
Rafra!

00:15:57.490 --> 00:15:58.850
You're okay!

00:15:59.590 --> 00:16:01.860
What's the distortion in this area?

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:04.630
I understand it to be due to the
function outlined in the report.

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:05.590
I see.

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:07.560
We could be in trouble if
they're able to utilize it.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:13.430
Is this the bridge?

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:17.170
We've finished transferring everyone
from Liebel. Please close the hatch.

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:18.140
<i>Roger.</i>

00:16:19.070 --> 00:16:21.140
I am exhausted.

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:23.270
We've hardly had any sleep, after all.

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:26.350
- Right. Ju...!
- Juli. You girls should get a room and rest.

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:27.080
Um... but...

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:30.740
All that's left to do is wait for the rescuers.
Ran, Carabona, that goes for you too.

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.550
Thank you. I think we'll do that.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.690
What'll we do about the criminals?

00:16:36.690 --> 00:16:39.060
We'd be wise to bring them over later.

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:43.060
Y-You're right. Please look after that.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:46.000
- So huge.
- Show me the map.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.970
This is nothing like Liebel.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:50.600
What's this?

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:52.870
So this is the container path.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:57.610
There's not enough room!

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:04.190
Wow. This isn't bad.

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:06.150
Yahoo!

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:10.220
Let's hurry and decide. I'm getting bored.

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:13.480
You're right. Looks like no one's
decided on a spot yet in this area.

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:15.260
Any preference?

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:16.530
Anywhere will do.

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:19.200
Then here. And the room across
the hall is still open as well.

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:21.290
Aoi. There's no door.

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:25.910
Well, it's the same everywhere. We'd
better take turns guarding the door.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:28.170
I've got some crime prevention tools.

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:32.310
We're across the hall from you, so
you've got nothing to worry about.

00:17:32.310 --> 00:17:33.780
<i>That's</i> what I'm worried about.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:34.850
Is that so!

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:37.020
Ikumi, will you protect me?

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:38.450
Leave it to me!

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:40.420
Then we girls are in here.

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:45.930
Akihiro! Take care of my luggage!
I'm gonna explore this ship! Yahoo!

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:48.730
Boy, that little kid is full of energy.

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:52.560
Ikumi, I'm gonna get us registered.

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:56.130
Then Akihiro and I will carry
our luggage into our room.

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:58.130
Thanks.

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:04.750
So here you are.

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:10.780
Pat... Campbell, right?

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:16.020
You're Instructor
Campbell's son, aren't you?

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:22.560
Did my daddy die?

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:29.800
Yes. But it's because of your daddy and the
other instructors that we're still alive.

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:35.640
I wanna go home.

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:38.510
So do I.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:40.500
Don't worry. We'll be able to go home.

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:46.080
But it looks like it'll take us more
time. Let's try to be patient until then.

00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:49.720
Where are we going?

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:52.780
The only room fit for us is
the officers' room, right?

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:53.960
Why's that?

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:57.400
We're the ones navigating this ship.
And that room has a door to it.

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:01.100
It's times like these that we must make
our position within the ship clear.

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:04.970
What do you want, shorty?

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:06.370
Hi Charlie.

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:07.270
Hi.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:09.110
Hi.

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:10.080
H-Hi.

00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:14.250
Excuse us!

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:17.090
Make our position clear?

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:19.650
Let's hurry to the bridge.

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:21.820
What's with the "Charlie"?

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:25.560
A-A nickname. I'm quite
friendly with them.

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:26.660
Really.

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:29.400
Team registration is being handled
here. Please line up in a single line.

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:32.030
While waiting, get your ID numbers
and residence number handy.

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:37.900
The bridge is undoubtedly
the place best suited to me.

00:19:38.710 --> 00:19:40.040
What are you doing, Kreis?

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:44.870
A simulation from when
we were in the Geduld?

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:48.940
We were pulled by something, weren't we?

00:19:49.550 --> 00:19:51.780
Right. We've gotta find out what.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:03.200
If she gives you trouble,
feel free to kick her out.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:05.530
U-Um, nice to meet you.

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:06.500
Bye.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:08.970
Thanks... Yuki.

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:12.470
You know, you're just like me.

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:15.730
Yuki.

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:18.410
So, we were being pulled by a ship.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:20.280
Can we find out the registry of the ship?

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:23.280
At the beginning of the data.

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:24.150
Rock!

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:27.290
Rock, paper, scissors! Rock, Paper, scissors!

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:28.590
Hi.

00:20:28.590 --> 00:20:30.220
I win!

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:31.660
Darn it!

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:33.090
What are they doing?

00:20:33.090 --> 00:20:34.560
Deciding who gets which bed.

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:36.620
Did you want something?

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:40.370
She's not with anyone yet.

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:44.340
She says she's also a conductor, so I
was wondering if she could join you.

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:46.270
Um... I...

00:20:46.270 --> 00:20:46.940
It's ok.

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:49.040
You can't be serious!

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:51.710
Okay. Please come in.

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:53.400
Aoi?

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:57.510
I'm Aoi Housen. Nice to meet you.

00:20:57.990 --> 00:20:59.950
I'm Faina.

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:07.790
So cute! What's an animal doing here?

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:10.000
I brought him with me.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:11.700
I'm surprised that they would allow it.

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:13.030
Really.

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:14.100
And what's his name?

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:14.970
Rafra.

00:21:14.970 --> 00:21:16.700
Hi Rafra!

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:19.840
She seems to be hungry.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.880
What do ferrets eat?

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.810
Well, they're carnivores, so...!

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:27.480
We'll need to register her to our room too!

00:21:27.480 --> 00:21:30.150
Oops! I forgot to register our team.

00:21:30.150 --> 00:21:31.880
Come on! What are you doing?

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:40.800
A Gestalt type submersible ship?

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:41.930
Which means...

00:21:41.930 --> 00:21:46.130
The Orbital Security Bureau? That's
gotta be a mistake. Check again.

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:48.100
Huh? But...!

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:52.670
Abend 1, Abend 2. Separate!

00:21:55.780 --> 00:21:58.240
Upon locating the Bratica,
switch to our capture plan.

00:22:02.120 --> 00:22:04.080
What is this?

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:11.780
In your dry eyes...

00:22:11.780 --> 00:22:16.850
...a silhouette appears

00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:21.560
The blue colored future...

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:27.650
...swayed and glittered

00:22:29.460 --> 00:22:37.710
Ah... No one wants...

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:46.310
...freedom out of pity

00:22:46.310 --> 00:22:54.760
Ah... To the days I feared...

00:22:54.760 --> 00:22:58.660
...that I'd end up hurting someone,

00:22:58.660 --> 00:23:05.030
goodbye

00:23:08.890 --> 00:23:10.720
Infinite Ryvius

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:11.420
Infinite Ryvius
Next episode: A Little Harmony

00:23:11.420 --> 00:23:12.020
Next episode: A Little Harmony

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:14.930
Next episode: A Little Harmony
Rescue will come, if we
remain patient a little longer.

00:23:14.930 --> 00:23:17.360
Next episode: A Little Harmony
Rescue will come. I'm sure of it.

00:23:17.360 --> 00:23:19.500
Next episode: A Little Harmony
As emotions in the form
of hope conflict,

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:20.870
Next episode: A Little Harmony
sharpness of the mind
becomes a weapon...

00:23:20.870 --> 00:23:23.100
Next episode: A Little Harmony
...and we begin hurting
the feelings of one another.

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:25.970
Next episode: A Little Harmony
The little harmony just
born among us begins to crumble.

00:23:25.970 --> 00:23:27.810
Next episode: A Little Harmony
Hope, in vain...!

00:23:27.810 --> 00:23:29.040
Next episode: A Little Harmony
